{{!-- footer-lesson.hbs — the reading surface's footer.

     A lesson has its own chrome (.ns-coursenav at the top, the docked
     prev/next at the foot of the article), so this is deliberately the
     thinnest thing that still closes the page: the sponsor band, then the
     system's `.ns-footer__bar` — the same legal strip the full footer ends
     with, so the two do not disagree about what the bottom of the site is.

     No columns, no newsletter, no nav: everything a reader might leave for is
     already one control away in the bar above the lesson. --}}
{{> "ads/leaderboard"}}

<footer class="ns-footer">
  <div class="ns-footer__bar">
    <a href="{{@site.url}}">{{@site.title}}</a>
    <span class="ns-footer__spacer"></span>
    <span>&copy; {{date format="YYYY"}}</span>
    {{#has tag="#training-content"}}
      <a href="/training/">{{> icons name="map-trifold"}}{{t "All training"}}</a>
    {{else}}
      <a href="/courses/">{{> icons name="squares-four"}}{{t "All courses"}}</a>
    {{/has}}
  </div>
</footer>
